From 26d072705916beb8ef7c657adf1afb05c16801fc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: 1aeo <github@1aeo.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 08:40:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 06/13] relay_metrics: Count onion service descriptor fetches
 and uploads

An HSDir answers every rejected descriptor upload with the same 400,
whether the descriptor didn't parse or validate, or it was valid but not
newer than the one in our cache, which happens without any fault when
several instances publish for the same onion address. Descriptor fetches
and refused single-hop requests aren't counted at all, so during a fetch
flood an operator can't tell cache hits from misses.

Add tor_relay_hsdir_get_total{action="success|not_found|single_hop"} and
tor_relay_hsdir_post_total{action="success|bad_url|invalid|not_newer|
single_hop"}, in the same way as tor_relay_intro1_total. To tell
"invalid" from "not_newer", make hs_cache_store_as_dir() return -2 when
the descriptor is valid but not newer; its only caller checks for a
negative value. Only tunneled (BEGIN_DIR) requests are counted.

Part of #41339.
